--TEST--
`{previous: $e}` chains one throwable to the one that caused it, and an exception built without the bag reads `null` — spec § 10, `rule:core-api/shape-rules` R2's options shape
--FILE--
<?nvs
// Spec § 10: every exception is constructed the same way — one required
// message and one options shape. A subclass that declares no constructor of
// its own inherits the root's, bag included.
class ConfigError extends RuntimeError {
}

class Loader {
    public static function load(string $what): string {
        try {
            throw new IOError("no such file: " . $what);
        } catch (IOError $io) {
            throw new ConfigError("could not load " . $what, {previous: $io});
        }
    }
}

try {
    echo Loader::load("app.ini"), "\n";
} catch (Throwable $outer) {
    echo "outer=", $outer->message, "\n";
    // `previous` is `Throwable|null`, so a plain `->` reaches no member of it.
    // `?->` reads through it where it is written; narrowing is the other route
    // and wants a binding, a property being no narrowing subject —
    // `rule:types/narrowing`.
    echo "first=", $outer->previous?->message ?? "none", "\n";
    var $cause = $outer->previous;
    if ($cause == null) {
        echo "cause=none\n";
    } else {
        echo "cause=", $cause->message, "\n";
        // The chain stops here: the inner one was built with no bag at all,
        // which is the option's own `null` default.
        var $root = $cause->previous;
        if ($root == null) {
            echo "root=none\n";
        } else {
            echo "root=", $root->message, "\n";
        }
    }
}

// The bag is optional at every arity, and omitting it is not a diagnostic.
var $plain = new LogicError("nothing caused this");
var $none = $plain->previous;
if ($none == null) {
    echo "plain=none\n";
}
--EXPECT--
outer=could not load app.ini
first=no such file: app.ini
cause=no such file: app.ini
root=none
plain=none
